<title>JAPAN: Mitsui Mining raises zinc price 5,000 yen.</title>
<headline>Mitsui Mining raises zinc price 5,000 yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsui Mining and Smelting Co said on Thursday it had raised its selling price for zinc by 5,000 yen to 186,000 yen per tonne, effective immediately.</p>
<p>Major Japanese smelters periodically review their selling prices, changing them in line with market prices and currency rates.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
